.TH "MIRUCTL" "1" "2026\-08\-30" "Miru" "miructl Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
miructl \- control utility for miru\-daemon(1)
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBmiructl\fR <command>
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBmiructl\fR is a small, Wayland\-independent client.\& It connects to the Unix
socket created by \fBmiru\-daemon\fR(1) (\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/miru.\&sock\fR) and sends a
single command.\&
.PP
The daemon must already be running; otherwise \fBmiructl\fR fails with a
connection error.\&
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
\fBtoggle\fR
.RS 4
Show or hide the magnifier overlay.\& On first toggle the daemon captures
one frame and displays the zoomed view; a second toggle tears it down
(same as exiting with \fBEsc\fR when the in\-overlay help panel is closed).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBquit\fR
.RS 4
Ask \fBmiru\-daemon\fR to shut down.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print usage and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit (if supported by your build).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory containing \fBmiru.\&sock\fR (required for a normal session).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
# start the daemon (once per session), then:
miructl toggle
miructl quit
.PP
.RE
.SH SETTING UP A KEYBIND
.PP
Bind a compositor key to \fBmiructl toggle\fR (Niri, Hyprland, Sway, Mango, etc.\&).\&
Ensure \fBmiru\-daemon\fR is already running (e.\&g.\& as a systemd user service).\&
.PP
Examples and paths:
https://codeberg.\&org/Vaishnav\-Sabari\-Girish/miru#setting\-up\-a\-keybind
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBmiru\-daemon\fR(1)
.PP
